{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the probability of obtaining a favorable outcome, treating outcome differences as negligible. A 'favorable outcome' is not strictly defined but is interpreted as 'winning something' (i.e., a positive monetary outcome). For Lottery A: the probability of a favorable outcome is 50% (25% for 4000€ + 25% for 2000€). For Lottery B: the probability of a favorable outcome is 25% (only 25% for 6000€). Thus, Lottery A has a higher probability of a favorable outcome and would be preferred by this reason.",
